#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# head

#% text
# `head(x)` gives the head of a compound term `x`: `f` for `f(a, b)`, `list` for a list.
# For an atom it gives the name of its type: `Int`, `Rat`, `Float`, `Complex`, `Str` or `Sym`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Sums, products and powers have the heads `add`, `mul` and `pow`; `exp(x)` is the power `e^x`.

#% item
# The type names are the ones typed patterns use (`_: Int`).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
head(f(a, b))
#% output
#= f

#% cell
head([1, 2])
#% output
#= list

#% cell
head(x + y)
#% output
#= add

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Atoms give their type:

#% cell
map(head, [3, 2/3, 1.5, 1 + im, "s", x])
#% output
#= [Int, Rat, Float, Complex, Str, Sym]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `apply` with the head rebuilds the term:

#% cell
t = g(1, 2)
apply(head(t), [1, 2]) === t
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `apply`, `full_form`, `is_atom`, `length`
